<BaseLayout title="Swap Kits" description="Available LS swap kits for the Hyundai Genesis Coupe — mounts, oil pans, headers, and more.">
  <h1>Swap Kits</h1>

  <p>
    Several companies make bolt-in or near-bolt-in LS swap kits for the Genesis Coupe (BK1/BK2).
    The most common options cover motor mounts, oil pans, headers, and sometimes driveshafts or transmission mounts.
  </p>

  <h2>Sikky (most popular)</h2>
  <p>
    Sikky is the most widely used kit in the community. Their packages include high-quality motor mounts, transmission mount, aluminum race oil pan, headers, and optional driveshaft.
    Components are designed to work together and clear the subframe without hanging low.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.sikky.com/product/hyundai-genesis-lsx-swap-kit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Configurable kit builder</a> (start with mounts, add pan/headers/etc.)</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.sikky.com/product/sikky-2013-genesis-stage-2-ls-swap-kit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Stage 2 package</a> (mounts + pan + driveshaft + headers)</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.sikky.com/product/genesis-coupe-lsx-swap-front-sump-oil-pan-kit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oil pan</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.sikky.com/product/hyundai-genesis-ls1-headers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Headers</a> (1 7/8" primaries, stainless)</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
    Made in USA. Designed for LS1/LS2/LS3/LQ4/LQ9 and similar bolt patterns. Lifetime warranty on mounts.
  </p>

  <h2>LOJ Conversions (more adjustment)</h2>
  <p>
    LOJ mounts use slotted brackets that allow more fine-tuning of engine position than fixed designs.
    They also offer oil pans, transmission mounts, and complete kits for different transmissions.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://lojkits.com/collections/hyundai-genesis-coupe-bk-engine-swap-parts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LOJ Genesis Coupe collection</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://lojkits.com/products/genesis-coupe-lsx-swap-engine-mounts" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Motor mounts</a> (slotted for adjustment; BK1 includes drill template)</li>
    <li><a href="https://lojkits.com/products/genesis-coupe-lsx-basic-swap-kit" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Basic swap kits</a> (mounts + pan + other items depending on package)</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
    Useful when you need to shift the engine slightly for radiator, header, or accessory clearance.
  </p>

  <h2>ISR Performance (cheapest — caveats)</h2>
  <p>
    ISR offers the lowest-cost mount kit and separate headers. Community feedback is that the headers sit the lowest of the common options and are generally not recommended on powered (especially boosted) cars due to ground clearance and heat concerns.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.isrperformance.com/isr-performance-hyundai-genesis-ls-mount-kit/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ISR mount kit</a> (~$400)</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.isrperformance.com/isr-performance-ls-swap-headers-hyundai-genesis-coupe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ISR headers</a> (1 3/4" primaries — sit lowest)</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">
    Budget option for mounts only. Headers are a common point of complaint on higher-power builds.
  </p>

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Most kits are designed around a specific oil pan and mount combination — mixing brands can affect clearance.</li>
    <li>BK1 (2008–2012) and BK2 (2013–2016) have slightly different subframe mount holes; LOJ and some others note this and include a drill template for BK1.</li>
    <li>Always verify current pricing and fitment on the manufacturer sites — options and bundles change.</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
